  v_n0["CameraConfiguration::validat<br/>e() may adjust the camera <br/>configuration to the <br/>closest valid configuration <br/>and returns the validation <br/>status."]
  v_n1["Invalid means the <br/>configuration is invalid <br/>and cannot be adjusted. It <br/>may occur only in extreme <br/>cases, such as an empty <br/>configuration."]
  v_n2["Adjusted means the <br/>configuration has been <br/>adjusted and is now valid. <br/>Parameters for any stream <br/>may have changed and stream <br/>configurations may have <br/>been removed, so the caller <br/>must check the <br/>configuration carefully."]
  v_n3["Valid means the <br/>configuration was already <br/>valid and has not been <br/>adjusted."]
  v_n0 -->|"It may return Invalid."| v_n1
  v_n0 -->|"It may return Adjusted."| v_n2
  v_n0 -->|"It may return Valid."| v_n3
